{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrvrVGxnMvwLs721U5js","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`resolver/solve.py` is implemented and the 21 tests in `tests/test_solve.py` pass (`python3 tests/test_solve.py`).\n\nThe resolver does a depth-first search that always decides the alphabetically smallest unassigned package next, tries its versions newest first, and backtracks on conflict. It also checks cycle back-edges against already-chosen versions, and forward-checks that every pending package still has a candidate. `ResolutionError` names the package whose candidates ran out first, or the missing package. `Version` and `Constraint` are implemented as the spec describes.\n\nThings to know:\n- **Preference order is approximate in one case.** The search follows the spec's \"alphabetical, highest first\" rule, but it does not enumerate every solution to find the global lexicographic maximum. A package that only becomes reachable after a choice can, in rare cases, be decided later than a strict global ordering would require. I did not construct a counterexample.\n- **Three of my initial test expectations were wrong**, not the resolver. I corrected them after checking each by hand: `b` can take 3.0 in the alphabetical test, `leaf` takes 2.0 in the backtracking test, and `b` drops to 1.0 in the cycle test. I also added a forced-backtracking test.\n- **The \"few hundred versions\" test is weak.** It runs a layered chain with 200 versions per package and finishes quickly, but it doesn't force much backtracking. I did not benchmark a harder adversarial index.\n- Nothing is committed. The tests import the package via a path insert, since `tests/` has no `__init__.py`, so `python3 -m unittest discover` won't find them; run the file directly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3404,"cache_read_input_tokens":46823,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3404},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d5a9830-31bd-4ba3-afe2-098f86021f7f","uuid":"517eaeef-b467-48a7-a0de-23ac8999425e","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:50:48.587Z","request_id":"req_011CfrvrUpvcegrLbeEWuxBF"}
